{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791591576,"nonce":"kefqV9QOjLP0r/ksAgFNY9wd3CY=","message":"Update from the blinc_abi side (2026-10-10, relayed by another session): borders now take layout space in blinc_abi 3db5b2d (their issue aec21d4). Owned contexts already wrote Taffy's border in set_border, so blinc_ts geometry should not change; this was not re-checked here. blinc_ts builds against the ../blinc_abi path dependency and CI pins a commit, and neither pin has been moved for this.\n\nTaffy bug to design around: an absolute child with inset: 0 and margin: auto inside a bordered box is placed off-centre. In an 18px box with a 2px border it lands at 6,6 where CSS gives 4,4, because Taffy measures the insets from the padding box and resolves auto margins over the border box. Centre marks and icons inside bordered controls with the parent's align-items and justify-content and no insets.\n\nFor this issue: the notch-with-border test should be written against the new border behaviour, and a notch body inset by concave corners with a border on it is exactly where this off-centre placement would show.","files":null}]}